craftableCreatures.guide.page3.chapter=Chapter 1, Introduction
craftableCreatures.guide.page3.mainText.1=Welcome to Craftable Creatures, mod created to provide player ability to summon mobs in survival mode!\n<e>\nProgrammer: Wertyfire\nTextures: Wertyfire\n<e>\nMod's source code can be found on GitHub (link: https://github.com/Wertyfire/CraftableCreatures).
craftableCreatures.guide.page3.mainText.2=If you have wishes or you found a bug please report on GitHub.
craftableCreatures.guide.page4.chapter=Chapter 2, Souls
craftableCreatures.guide.page4.mainText.1=Souls are one of the main elements of mod. There are 25 souls - 24 of each mob and one of player.\nPlayer's soul appears in the place where he dies and the rest can be obtained with the help of soul extractor (see ch. 5).
craftableCreatures.guide.page4.mainText.2=<empty>
craftableCreatures.guide.page5.chapter=Chapter 3, Other Items
craftableCreatures.guide.page5.mainText.1=In addition to souls, there are also other items.\n
craftableCreatures.guide.page5.mainText.2=Bluestone is an important resource. It can be obtained by mining bluestone ore.\n\nBluestone is used in craft of Blueprints and evolved in craft of Soul Extractor and Combiner.
craftableCreatures.guide.page5.mainText.3=Blueprint is another item.\nIt can be crafted using paper and bluestone and it is needed to craft a Spawn Egg Blueprint.
craftableCreatures.guide.page5.mainText.4=Spawn Egg Blueprint required to combine items into Spawn Eggs in Combiner (see ch. 6).
craftableCreatures.guide.page5.mainText.5=Bat Wing drops out of Bat and is needed only to create Spawn Egg.
craftableCreatures.guide.page5.mainText.6=Ocelot Tail is also only needed to create Spawn Egg.
craftableCreatures.guide.page5.mainText.7=Transmutator can morph you into any mob, you just have to put it's soul in transmutator. §cMod Morph by iChun is required in order to use transmutator.
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.chapter=Chapter 4, Blocks
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.1=There are 2 types of blocks: usual and functional. Functional are blocks with interface, usual is all others.
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.2=Usual Blocks
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.3=Bluestone Ore is a block that is generated underground. When mined, it drops Bluestone.
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.4=Bluestone Block used for convenient storage of Bluestone.
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.5=Powered\nBluestone Block
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.6=Powered Bluestone Block due to it's magical properties emits redstone signal.
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.7=Functional Blocks
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.8=Soul Extractor extracts\nthe soul from a mob-related item and inserts it into usual soul. You can see it's interface below.
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.9=Combiner transforms\nthe soul into an item according to the blueprint (into a spawn egg). It's interface present below.
craftableCreatures.guide.page6.mainText.10=These are currently the only blocks available in the mod.
craftableCreatures.guide.page7.chapter=Chapter 5, Soul Extractor
craftableCreatures.guide.page7.mainText.1=When mob dies, part of its soul remains in item it drops. Soul Extractor is needed to extract the soul from this item. In addition to the item, in the mechanism you need to place a regular soul, which will contain the mob's soul.
craftableCreatures.guide.page7.mainText.2=You need to use a bluestone as fuel, as it has magical properties and helps extract the soul.
craftableCreatures.guide.page7.mainText.3=The following is a recipe\nfor a Soul Extractor
craftableCreatures.guide.page8.chapter=Chapter 6, Combiner
craftableCreatures.guide.page8.mainText.1=Combiner is needed to create a Spawn Egg.
craftableCreatures.guide.page8.mainText.2=It does not require fuel, as it is powered by the Redstone Block used to create this Combiner.
craftableCreatures.guide.page8.mainText.3=Here is the Combiner's recipe:
